  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IATI Data Validator Service</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Both DfiD and MoFA have established guidelines for International Development Organisations who need to publish their data in the IATI format. There is not yet a software tool available to automatically validate this data against the guidelines in order to help IATI data publishers to improve their data quality. Because of this a validator service tool should be developed and hosted.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development and hosting of an IATI Data Validation service</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IATI publishers</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objectives of developing the IATI Data Validator Service are:
Guaranteeing a minimum level of quality of IATI data before these are used to monitor the progress of International Development activities.
Making software available for IATI publishers to use and to check their data quality, reducing manual workload
Supporting the Ministry in providing feedback on quality issues</narrative>
  </description>
